# Build config. The SDK auto-discovers ./source and ./resources by convention,
# INCLUDING resource qualifiers like ./resources-<device> and ./resources-spa, so
# pointing at the manifest is enough.
#
# Launcher icons: each device has its own resources-<device>/drawables/ with a
# correctly-sized icon plus its own drawable definition (auto-discovered by the
# device qualifier). There is deliberately NO icon in the base resources/ -- a base
# icon would be overridden by every device and the packager would warn about it. The
# base resources/ holds only shared, size-independent resources (strings, settings).
project.manifest = manifest.xml
